Looking at the error "At least one statement is expected", the issue is having two consecutive `VAR` sections in CODESYS. The compiler doesn't allow multiple `VAR` blocks of the same type; temporary variables should be merged with the persistent state variables.

```json
{"edits":[{"old":"VAR
    prevLeadPump    : INT := 0;
    prevLagPump     : INT := 0;
    prevRunningCount : INT := 0;
    prevClippedDemand : INT := 0;
    wasDemandZero   : BOOL := TRUE;
END_VAR

VAR
    clippedDemand : INT;
    tmp_i         : INT;
    tmp_minHours  : LINT;
    tmp_minPump   : INT;
    tmp_secondMinHours : LINT;
    tmp_secondMinPump  : INT;
    tmp_mainHoursDiff  : LINT;
END_VAR

    // PUB001: Clip demand to 0..5", "new":"VAR
    prevLeadPump    : INT := 0;
    prevLagPump     : INT := 0;
    prevRunningCount : INT := 0;
    prevClippedDemand : INT := 0;
    wasDemandZero   : BOOL := TRUE;
    clippedDemand : INT;
    tmp_i         : INT;
    tmp_minHours  : LINT;
    tmp_minPump   : INT;
    tmp_secondMinHours : LINT;
    tmp_secondMinPump  : INT;
    tmp_mainHoursDiff  : LINT;
END_VAR

    // PUB001: Clip demand to 0..5"}]}
```
